{
  "summary": "This experiment tested whether aggregating multiple profiles via average pooling (multiprofile + avgpool) in the RNA-only, scVI_n200 setting captures complementary per-profile signal beyond a single profile, constituting a single conceptual change from llm_summary_004 (RNA-only, singleprofile, scVI_n200, no aggregation). The configuration achieved a validation accuracy of 0.650 (F1 0.628), a substantial ~13% improvement over the singleprofile scVI baseline (0.520, F1 0.498), indicating that multiprofile aggregation captures meaningful complementary signal that a single profile discards. It remains uncertain whether this gain is specific to average pooling versus other aggregation strategies, whether the improvement is stable across repeated runs, and whether the advantage transfers to multimodal or alternative-fusion configurations."
}

